This position has a selective placement factor that will be used to screen out ineligible candidates. The selective placement factor is: You must currently be a licensed Professional Engineer (PE) if applying for the 0810 or 830 series. Your license must be held in a State, the District of Columbia, the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, or a territory of the United States. Please submit the applicable license with your application package. In addition to the Basic Requirements for this position, your resume must also demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-12 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: 1) Providing technical references, guidance, training mentorship to colleagues and PWD staff in DoD planning criteria, master planning, facility planning, economic analyses, explosive safety siting, Asset Evaluations, Basic Facility Requirements, and space management;
2) Directing a full range of projects associated with managing facilities, land and other resources;
3) Developing training requirements and working with employees to develop Individual Development Plans;
4) Planning, coordinating, prioritizing and directing activities of engineers/architects, planners and planner techs in the performance of Asset Management products & services; and
5) Constructing, managing, and maintaining facilities, land, and other assets within a military installation. NOTE: THIS INFORMATION MUST BE SUPPORTED IN YOUR RESUME TO BE CONSIDERED FOR THE POSITION. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website: Community Planning Series 0020 (opm.gov)
